  "controlled": "Reasons are the vocabulary of every change callback: onValueChange/onOpenChange/onSelectedChange etc. report one of these strings in eventDetails.reason. Component-specific subsets exist (e.g. Tabs.Root.ChangeEventReason = 'none' | 'disabled' | 'missing' | 'initial').",
  "formIntegration": null,
  "keyboard": "'list-navigation' and 'keyboard' reasons let a consumer distinguish arrow-key driven changes from typed input.",
  "notableDifferences": [
    "React Aria does not surface a reason vocabulary on change callbacks; it provides separate callbacks (onPress/onChange/onSelectionChange) and PressEvent types. The reason string is the Base UI mechanism for the same distinction and must be used when migrating logic that branched on RAC callback identity (e.g. distinguishing a programmatic value change from a user one)."
